## Summary

Adds optimization mode for invariant testing, similar to Echidna. This mode maximizes an `int256` return value from an `invariant*` function.

Closes #12190

## Usage

Define an invariant function returning `int256` :

```solidity
function invariant_optimize_maxRoundingError() external view returns (int256) {
    return int256(pool.totalShares()) - int256(pool.expectedShares());
}
```

- Foundry will fuzz to find the sequence that maximizes this value
- The best value and sequence are tracked and reported
- Sequence shrinking is applied to find the minimal reproducing sequence

```solidity

contract InvariantOptimizer is Test {
    int256 maxPriceDifference;

    function setUp() public {
        targetContract(address(this));
    }

    function setMaxPriceDifference(uint256 startPrice, uint256 endPrice, uint256 startTime, uint256 endTime) public {
        /// logic to set maxPriceDifference here
    }

    function invariant_opt_price_difference() public view returns (int256) {
        return maxPriceDifference;
    }
}

[PASS]
	[Best sequence] (original: 392, shrunk: 1)
		vm.warp(block.timestamp + 123408035);
		vm.prank(0x7FA9385bE102ac3EAc297483Dd6233D62b3e1496);
		InvariantOptimizer(0x7FA9385bE102ac3EAc297483Dd6233D62b3e1496).setMaxPriceDifference(115792089237316195423570985008687907853269984665640564039457584007913129639933, 115792089210356248756420345214020892766250353992003419616917011526809519390721, 2230, 3400);
 invariant_opt_price_difference() (best: 2843574705161656291476921143606979357380022738070982514754023847085364228, runs: 256, calls: 128000)
```

## Bug fix during implementation

Fixed a bug in shrink logic where `vm.warp` and `vm.roll` values were not correctly accumulated when replaying shrunk sequences. This caused the "best" sequence to be non-reproducible because time/block values depended on removed calls.

The fix:
- Keeps reverted calls in sequence during optimization to preserve warp/roll
- Accumulates warps/rolls from removed calls into kept calls during shrinking
- Updates inspector's cheatcodes.block alongside executor.env

## Tests

- `invariant_optimization_mode` - basic optimization with deterministic increment
- `invariant_optimization_negative_values` - optimization starting from negative values
- `invariant_optimization_with_warp` - warp-based optimization with shrunk sequence output (fixed seed)

This PR adds checks for critical errors in the replica and replica restarts at the end of every system test (group) unless explicitly turned off.

Checks for critical errors are turned off for `dual_workload_test` and `max_xnet_payload_size_test` which use invalid payload sizes.

Checks for replica restarts are turned off for tests performing:
- subnet recovery;
- topology changes;
- failed state divergence checks;
- `guestos_recovery_engine_smoke_test` (that does not wait for the replica process to even come up).

Note that this PR does not fully cover critical errors and replica restarts in tests that kill and/or reboot a node (since this PR only performs the checks at the end of the test and not before every reboot).
Moreover, checks are skipped on nodes from which metrics cannot be scraped (making the assumption for now that such nodes have been killed deliberately).
